{"content":[{"c":["SHEMA*, The"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["The declaration “Hear, O Israel, Yahweh our God is one Yahweh” (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.6.4","r":"Deut.6.4","rawR":"Deut.6.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.6.4","value":"Deut.6.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 6:4"},"). ",{"c":["Shema"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"}," comes from the first Hebrew word of the verse, ",{"c":["shema"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," “hear.” Verses ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.6.4-9","r":"Deut.6.4-9","rawR":"Deut.6.4-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.6.4-9","value":"Deut.6.4-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"4-9"}," make up the whole of this foundational biblical truth. While several translations of verse ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.6.4","r":"Deut.6.4","rawR":"Deut.6.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.6.4","value":"Deut.6.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"4"}," are grammatically correct, Jesus’ words in ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.12.29","r":"Mark.12.29","rawR":"Mark.12.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.12.29","value":"Mark.12.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mark 12:29"}," correspond most closely to the one given above. Religious Jews recite the Shema three times daily as part of their devotional life; no Sabbath worship is conducted in the synagogue without its proclamation."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Within the Shema is found both a fundamental doctrinal truth and a resultant obligation. There is an urgency connected to the teaching: the word ",{"c":["shema"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"}," demands that the hearer respond with his total being to the fact and demands of this essential revelation."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["With regard to the teaching pertaining to the nature of God, the word “one” (",{"c":["echad"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"},") designates a compound unity rather than an absolute singular. While the eminent medieval Jewish theologian Maimonides insisted that God was ",{"c":["yachid"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"}," (an absolute singular), the OT does not use this word to define God’s nature. The compound singular word for “one” first occurs in ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.2.24","r":"Gen.2.24","rawR":"Gen.2.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.2.24","value":"Gen.2.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Genesis 2:24"}," where a man and woman, though separate entities, are seen to be one (",{"c":["echad"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"},") in marriage. Understandably, Jesus could freely quote ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.6.4","r":"Deut.6.4","rawR":"Deut.6.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.6.4","value":"Deut.6.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Deuteronomy 6:4"}," without infringing upon the truth of his own deity."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=DeuteronomyBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"DeuteronomyBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"DeuteronomyBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Deuteronomy, Book of"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Shemathe","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dt 6:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.6.4","rawQueryValue":"Deut.6.4","sourceRefExact":"Deut.6.4"},{"anchorText":"4-9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.6.4-9","rawQueryValue":"Deut.6.4-9","sourceRefExact":"Deut.6.4-9"},{"anchorText":"4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.6.4","rawQueryValue":"Deut.6.4","sourceRefExact":"Deut.6.4"},{"anchorText":"Mark 12:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.12.29","rawQueryValue":"Mark.12.29","sourceRefExact":"Mark.12.29"},{"anchorText":"Genesis 2:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.2.24","rawQueryValue":"Gen.2.24","sourceRefExact":"Gen.2.24"},{"anchorText":"Deuteronomy 6:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.6.4","rawQueryValue":"Deut.6.4","sourceRefExact":"Deut.6.4"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"0701c8bd7d3f5928263f17080b40e093034ecc63729f9177f976cc3c79e8ec4e","sourceItemName":"Shemathe","sourceItemOrder":271,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Shemathe","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Shema*, the","title":"Shema*, the","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}